{% doc %}
  Resolve a tool name to its validated manifest (spec §9.2 step 4). Only tools in
  the built registry (explicitly registered + meta-schema-valid) are resolvable —
  an unregistered or excluded tool is simply not found, so the surface can never
  execute an unvalidated action.

  Two narrowings, both of which can only take tools away (§6.2):

  - `allowed_tools`, when non-empty, intersects the served set. Per TOKEN.
  - the person's per-AGENT switches (queries/agents/tool_enabled), when
    `user_id` and `client_id` are given. Per agent, so it survives the OAuth
    refresh that replaces a token's digests.

  They accumulate: a tool a token allows but the person switched off for that
  agent is not resolvable. Neither can widen the other.

  A narrowed-away tool is reported as NOT FOUND, exactly as an unregistered one
  is, rather than announcing that it exists but is forbidden — least disclosure,
  and the behaviour `allowed_tools` already had.

  `approval/execute` passes no identity here on purpose: on that path the
  credential is re-checked by identity/token_still_authorized, which applies
  both narrowings itself.

  @param {string} name            - requested tool name
  @param {array}  [allowed_tools] - per-token narrowing (nil/empty = all)
  @param {string} [user_id]       - principal user id, for the per-agent switches
  @param {string} [client_id]     - agent key (helpers/identity/agent_key)
  @return {object|null} the manifest, or null if not resolvable
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  if allowed_tools != blank and allowed_tools != empty
    unless allowed_tools contains name
      return null
    endunless
  endif

  if user_id != blank and client_id != blank
    function switched_on = 'modules/mcp/queries/agents/tool_enabled', user_id: user_id, client_id: client_id, tool_name: name
    unless switched_on
      return null
    endunless
  endif

  function reg = 'modules/mcp/queries/registry/load'
  assign found = null
  for m in reg.tools
    if m.name == name
      assign found = m
      break
    endif
  endfor
  return found
%}
